---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Methodology — CGEL Database"
  description="How CGEL initiatives are selected and coded: unit of analysis, inclusion criteria, governance levels, initiative types, and the IISD environmental typology."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 class="serif">Methodology</h2>
        <p>
          A summary of how initiatives are selected and coded. The full codebook
          is available to download.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="dlcard">
        <div>
          <div class="dltitle">Full Codebook &amp; Methodology (v1.0)</div>
          <div class="dlsub">
            29 variables, governance-level definitions, initiative-type coding,
            IISD environmental typology, data conventions · Word document
          </div>
        </div>
        <a
          class="dlbtn"
          href="/assets/docs/CGEL_Codebook_Methodology_v1.docx"
          download
          >↓ Download .docx</a
        >
      </div>

      <h3>Unit of analysis &amp; inclusion criteria</h3>
      <p>
        The unit of analysis is a <strong>governance initiative</strong> — an
        institutionalised arrangement that involves <em>steering</em> and is
        recognised as <em>authoritative</em> by its network, rather than mere
        lip service. An initiative is included when it meets all of the
        following:
      </p>
      <div class="criteria">
        <div class="crit">
          <div class="num">1</div>
          <div class="txt">
            Active during <strong>2000–2024</strong> (including cases that began
            before 2000 or ended before 2025).
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="crit">
          <div class="num">2</div>
          <div class="txt">
            Involves <strong>substantial action</strong> — steering, and
            authority recognised by its constituent actors.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="crit">
          <div class="num">3</div>
          <div class="txt">
            Primarily aims to <strong>address environmental issues</strong>, or
            has them as a key concern.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="crit">
          <div class="num">4</div>
          <div class="txt">
            Operates at
            <strong>multilateral, bilateral, or transnational</strong>
            level; involves non-Chinese actors and activity beyond China's
            borders.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="crit">
          <div class="num">5</div>
          <div class="txt">
            <strong>(Co-)created or mainly led</strong>
            by Chinese actors.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Governance levels</h3>
      <p>
        Each initiative is classified as
        <strong>transnational</strong>
        (non-state actors and networks, decentralised),
        <strong>multilateral</strong>
        (states and IGOs, treaty-based, &gt;2 countries), or
        <strong>bilateral</strong>
        (two states, formal agreements).
      </p>

      <h3>Initiative types (governance functions)</h3>
      <p>
        Initiatives are coded into up to three of six functional types, ordered
        by importance: (1) information sharing and dialogues; (2)
        capacity-building and training; (3) direct action and demonstration; (4)
        provision of funding; (5) research and scientific knowledge production;
        (6) rule-making and standard-setting.
      </p>

      <h3>Environmental problems</h3>
      <p>
        Up to two primary problems are coded from the IISD typology (climate
        change, energy, water, biodiversity, atmosphere, oceans &amp; coasts,
        forests, agriculture &amp; food security, chemicals &amp; wastes,
        cities, disaster &amp; humanitarian relief). Initiatives spanning three
        or more problems are flagged as addressing
        <em>broad environmental issues</em>.
      </p>

      <h3>Map aggregation rule</h3>
      <p>
        The collaboration map shades each country by the number of initiatives
        in which it is the
        <strong>primary international collaborator</strong>
        (Variable 23, origin per the World Bank country list). Multi-country
        collaborators are split and counted once each.
        <span class="placeholder"
          >[待补：是否在地图中排除以 China 为合作方来源的少数记录]</span
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
